<DocsLayout title="Configuration and policy" description="Configure analyzers, gates, quality thresholds, and reviewed suppressions.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE</p><h1>Configuration and policy</h1><p class="lede">Keep scan behavior and risk acceptance reviewable in version control. VulnWeave separates scan configuration from the policy that can fail a gate.</p>
    <h2>Project configuration</h2><p><code>vulnweave.config.json</code> selects analyzers, rules, and the baseline policy. CLI options take precedence for one-off runs.</p><pre><code>&#123;&#10;  "schemaVersion": 1,&#10;  "analyzer": "all",&#10;  "semgrepConfig": "rules/vulnweave-starter.yml",&#10;  "baselinePolicy": "vulnweave.baseline.json",&#10;  "gitleaksConfig": ".gitleaks.toml"&#10;&#125;</code></pre>
    <h2>Security baseline and suppressions</h2><p><code>vulnweave.baseline.json</code> holds the gate threshold, required-analyzer rule, and approved time-limited exceptions. A suppression remains visible in reports but does not count toward the severity gate until it expires.</p><pre><code>&#123;&#10;  "schemaVersion": 1,&#10;  "failOn": "high",&#10;  "requireAnalyzers": true,&#10;  "suppressions": [&#123;&#10;    "fingerprint": "scanner-stable-fingerprint",&#10;    "reason": "Accepted until the upstream upgrade window.",&#10;    "owner": "team@example.com",&#10;    "expiresOn": "2026-12-31"&#10;  &#125;]&#10;&#125;</code></pre><p>Do not use a suppression as a permanent hiding mechanism. Every entry needs a specific fingerprint, reason, owner, and expiry date.</p>
    <h2>Quality thresholds and optional gate</h2><p>Quality remains advisory by default. Tune it to project conventions first, then only enable a quality gate after reviewing the baseline.</p><pre><code>&#123;&#10;  "quality": &#123;&#10;    "complexityThreshold": 12,&#10;    "duplicateBlockLines": 8,&#10;    "nestingThreshold": 4,&#10;    "functionLineThreshold": 60,&#10;    "parameterThreshold": 5&#10;  &#125;,&#10;  "qualityGate": &#123;&#10;    "maxComplexitySignals": 8,&#10;    "maxDuplicateCodeSignals": 2,&#10;    "maxUnreferencedFiles": 0&#10;  &#125;&#10;&#125;</code></pre><p>Unreferenced-file signals observe local static JavaScript/TypeScript imports only. They do not prove that a file is dead code.</p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
